<div class="text">
    <p><span style="font-weight: 400;">If you want to stand out from the crowd, you have the option to adorn your body with a plethora of interesting drawings and patterns.</span><span style="font-weight: 400;"></span><span style="font-weight: 400;">There are over <strong>500 different tattoos</strong> available for you to choose from, which can be applied all over your body from head to toe.</span></p>
    <p><span style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>To get a tattoo</strong>, you should enter a tattoo parlor and stand on the designated "<strong>Marker</strong>", then press "<strong>E</strong>" and a menu will open for you to choose the location and tattoo design.</span></p>
    <p><span style="font-weight: 400;">If you've decided to <strong>remove a tattoo</strong>, we recommend heading to the central hospital in Los Santos and locating an NPC in one of the rooms. With their assistance, you can <strong>remove tattoos</strong> from specific areas on your body. The cost of removing one tattoo is $300.</span></p>
