<div class="text">
    <p><font size="6"><center><span style="font-weight: 400;">Territory War (capture) and Business War (bizwar)</center></font> are criminal RP events in which faction members battle against another faction for control over a specific territory or business.<br><span style="font-weight: 400;"><br /></span><span style="font-weight: 400;"></span></p>
    <p><center>
        <span style="font-weight: 400;">
            <strong>Only mafia factions can fight for businesses:</strong><br />
            La Cosa Nostra, Russian Mafia, Yakuza, and Armenian Mafia.
        </span></center>
        <span style="font-weight: 400;"><br /></span>
        <center><span style="font-weight: 400;">
            <strong>Only gangs can fight for territories:</strong><br />
            Ballas, Families, Bloods, Vagos, and MG-13.
        </span></center>
        <span style="font-weight: 400;"><br /></span><span style="font-weight: 400;"></span>
    </p>
    <blockquote>
        <p>
            <span style="font-weight: 400;">
                In order to initiate a war, you need to use the command <b>/capture</b> or <b>/bizwar</b> in the appropriate location. To participate as a regular player, you must have the corresponding access in your faction tablet's settings.
            </span>
        </p>
        <p>
            <span style="font-weight: 400;">
                All capture and bizwar events take place in another dimension, which means they are out-of-character (OOC) events. This is why you have the opportunity to teleport to the zone only once using the commands <b>/tpcapture</b> and <b>/tpbizwar</b>.
                <br />
            </span>
            <span style="font-weight: 400;">For each territory or business, the entire faction receives $90 per hour, and</span>
<span style="font-weight: 400;">when all territories or businesses are captured, the faction leader is rewarded with a pleasant bonus for this achievement.</span>
        </p>
        <br />
    </blockquote>

        
